 it throws when the patch is invalid or an operation cannot be applied. Operations are evaluated in order,
 and evaluation stops at the first error. Neither the document nor the patch is mutated, so a failed patch
 does not expose a partially applied result.
+
+## JSON Merge Patch
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies an [RFC 7386 JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386)
+and returns a new JSON document. Object patches merge recursively; a member set to `null` is removed, while
+array and scalar patches replace the target. Neither input is mutated.
